---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Why Moment"
  description="Why teams choose Moment for domain-driven development. The problem with scattered domain knowledge and how temporal DDD modeling solves it."
>
  <Nav slot="nav" />

  <section class="why-hero">
    <div class="why-hero__inner">
      <h1 class="why-hero__title">Why Moment</h1>
      <p class="why-hero__subtitle">
        Domain-driven design produces better software. But without tooling, it produces
        scattered knowledge, untested flows, and documentation that lies.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ THE PROBLEM ============ -->
  <section class="why-section">
    <div class="why-section__inner">
      <h2 class="why-section__title">The problem</h2>
      <div class="why-narrative">
        <div class="why-narrative__block">
          <h3 class="why-narrative__heading">Domain knowledge fragments on contact with code</h3>
          <p>
            Your team runs an Event Storming. You map bounded contexts on a whiteboard.
            Then someone opens an IDE and starts writing types. Someone else writes tests.
            A third person updates the wiki. A fourth defines the API contract.
          </p>
          <p>
            By the end of the sprint, you have six representations of the same domain model.
            They already disagree.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-narrative__block">
          <h3 class="why-narrative__heading">Flows are the untested frontier</h3>
          <p>
            Most teams test individual commands and queries. Very few test the flows between
            bounded contexts &mdash; the temporal sequences where events cross boundaries,
            contracts are exchanged, and sagas coordinate long-running processes.
          </p>
          <p>
            These flows are where the hardest bugs live: race conditions, broken contracts,
            missing compensation logic, and orphaned events. And they're exactly what
            nobody writes tests for.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-narrative__block">
          <h3 class="why-narrative__heading">Boilerplate doesn't scale</h3>
          <p>
            Every new aggregate means writing TypeScript interfaces, aggregate classes,
            test stubs, Gherkin scenarios, specification documents, and API contracts.
            Multiply by every bounded context. Multiply by every change.
          </p>
          <p>
            The cost isn't just time &mdash; it's drift. Manual artifacts diverge from
            intent. Tests cover the wrong cases. Documentation describes last month's model.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ THE SOLUTION ============ -->
  <section class="why-section why-section--alt">
    <div class="why-section__inner">
      <h2 class="why-section__title">How Moment solves it</h2>
      <div class="why-solution">
        <div class="why-solution__item">
          <div class="why-solution__number">1</div>
          <div class="why-solution__body">
            <h3 class="why-solution__heading">Single source of truth</h3>
            <p>
              The <code>.moment</code> specification is the canonical definition of your domain.
              Contexts, aggregates, commands, events, flows, crossings, sagas, policies &mdash;
              all in one file, in one language, version-controlled alongside your code.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="why-solution__item">
          <div class="why-solution__number">2</div>
          <div class="why-solution__body">
            <h3 class="why-solution__heading">Temporal modeling with flows</h3>
            <p>
              Flows define how events move through time across bounded contexts. Lanes,
              moments, branches, crossings with contracts, <code>triggered-by</code> chains,
              and terminal states make the temporal dimension explicit and testable.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="why-solution__item">
          <div class="why-solution__number">3</div>
          <div class="why-solution__body">
            <h3 class="why-solution__heading">Deterministic artifact generation</h3>
            <p>
              Same input, same output. Every time. TypeScript types with discriminated unions,
              test scaffolds with crossing assertions, Gherkin features with flow coverage,
              spec docs with Mermaid diagrams, and AsyncAPI contracts. Six artifact types
              from one specification.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="why-solution__item">
          <div class="why-solution__number">4</div>
          <div class="why-solution__body">
            <h3 class="why-solution__heading">Drift detection closes the loop</h3>
            <p>
              <code>moment drift</code> compares your specification against implementation
              using AST-level diffing. When they diverge, you know exactly what changed,
              where, and why. Reconcile in either direction.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ COMPARISON TABLE ============ -->
  <section class="why-section">
    <div class="why-section__inner">
      <h2 class="why-section__title">How Moment compares</h2>
      <p class="why-section__subtitle">
        Moment isn't a code generator. It's a specification-driven toolchain
        that produces artifacts you'd write by hand &mdash; but can't keep in sync manually.
      </p>
      <div class="why-table-wrap">
        <table class="why-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th></th>
              <th>Manual DDD</th>
              <th>OpenAPI / Swagger</th>
              <th>GraphQL Schema-First</th>
              <th class="why-table__highlight">Moment</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="why-table__label">Source of truth</td>
              <td>Wiki + code + tests</td>
              <td>API spec (YAML)</td>
              <td>Schema (SDL)</td>
              <td class="why-table__highlight">.moment specification</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="why-table__label">Domain modeling</td>
              <td>Whiteboard / Event Storming</td>
              <td>Endpoints only</td>
              <td>Types only</td>
              <td class="why-table__highlight">Contexts, aggregates, flows, sagas, policies</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="why-table__label">Generates types</td>
              <td>Manual</td>
              <td>Yes</td>
              <td>Yes</td>
              <td class="why-table__highlight">Yes (discriminated unions, readonly)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="why-table__label">Generates tests</td>
              <td>Manual</td>
              <td>No</td>
              <td>No</td>
              <td class="why-table__highlight">Yes (scaffolds + Gherkin features)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="why-table__label">Generates docs</td>
              <td>Manual</td>
              <td>Swagger UI</td>
              <td>Schema introspection</td>
              <td class="why-table__highlight">Spec docs with Mermaid diagrams</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="why-table__label">Temporal flows</td>
              <td>Not modeled</td>
              <td>Not modeled</td>
              <td>Not modeled</td>
              <td class="why-table__highlight">First-class (lanes, crossings, branches)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="why-table__label">Drift detection</td>
              <td>None</td>
              <td>None</td>
              <td>None</td>
              <td class="why-table__highlight">AST-level diffing</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="why-table__label">Schema governance</td>
              <td>Manual versioning</td>
              <td>Version in URL</td>
              <td>Deprecation directives</td>
              <td class="why-table__highlight">4-phase lifecycle (Active → Deprecated → EOL → Removed)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ WHO IS THIS FOR ============ -->
  <section class="why-section why-section--alt">
    <div class="why-section__inner">
      <h2 class="why-section__title">Who Moment is for</h2>
      <div class="why-personas">
        <div class="why-persona">
          <h3 class="why-persona__role">Architects</h3>
          <ul class="why-persona__list">
            <li>Enforce bounded context boundaries with crossing contracts</li>
            <li>Govern schema evolution across teams with lifecycle policies</li>
            <li>Detect specification drift before it reaches production</li>
            <li>Visualize context maps and flow timelines from the spec</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="why-persona">
          <h3 class="why-persona__role">IC Engineers</h3>
          <ul class="why-persona__list">
            <li>Stop writing boilerplate types, tests, and docs by hand</li>
            <li>Get pre-populated test scaffolds with crossing assertions</li>
            <li>Trust that generated code matches the domain model</li>
            <li>Use watch mode for instant feedback during development</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="why-persona">
          <h3 class="why-persona__role">Team Leads</h3>
          <ul class="why-persona__list">
            <li>Onboard new engineers with a readable domain specification</li>
            <li>Ensure consistency across bounded contexts and teams</li>
            <li>Living documentation that never drifts from implementation</li>
            <li>Adopt incrementally, one context at a time</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ CTA ============ -->
  <section class="why-cta">
    <div class="why-cta__inner">
      <h2 class="why-cta__title">Ready to try it?</h2>
      <p class="why-cta__desc">
        Start with one bounded context. Write a <code>.moment</code> file.
        See what Moment generates.
      </p>
      <div class="why-cta__buttons">
        <a href="/get-started" class="btn btn--primary">Get Started</a>
        <a href="/examples" class="btn btn--secondary">See Examples</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Base>

<style>
  .why-hero {
    padding: var(--space-20) var(--space-6) var(--space-10);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .why-hero__inner { max-width: var(--content-width); margin: 0 auto; }
  .why-hero__title { font-size: var(--text-4xl); font-weight: var(--weight-bold); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .why-hero__subtitle { color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: var(--text-lg); max-width: 40rem; margin: 0 auto; line-height: var(--leading-relaxed); }

  .why-section { padding: var(--space-16) var(--space-6); }
  .why-section--alt { background: var(--color-surface); }
  .why-section__inner { max-width: var(--max-width); margin: 0 auto; }
  .why-section__title { font-size: var(--text-3xl); font-weight: var(--weight-bold); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .why-section__subtitle { color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: var(--text-lg); margin-bottom: var(--space-8); max-width: 40rem; }

  /* Narrative */
  .why-narrative { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-10); }
  .why-narrative__heading { font-size: var(--text-xl); font-weight: var(--weight-semibold); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .why-narrative__block p { color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: var(--leading-relaxed); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); max-width: 42rem; }

  /* Solution steps */
  .why-solution { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-8); }
  .why-solution__item { display: flex; gap: var(--space-5); }
  .why-solution__number {
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    width: 36px; height: 36px; flex-shrink: 0;
    background: var(--color-accent-muted); color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold); font-size: var(--text-lg);
    border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
  }
  .why-solution__heading { font-size: var(--text-lg); font-weight: var(--weight-semibold); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .why-solution__body p { color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: var(--leading-relaxed); max-width: 42rem; }
  .why-solution__body code { color: var(--color-accent); background: var(--color-accent-muted); padding: 0.1em 0.4em; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font-size: 0.9em; }

  /* Comparison table */
  .why-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin-top: var(--space-6); }
  .why-table {
    width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: var(--text-sm);
    min-width: 700px;
  }
  .why-table th {
    text-align: left; padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary); font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: var(--text-xs); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .why-table td {
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary); vertical-align: top;
  }
  .why-table__label { color: var(--color-text-primary) !important; font-weight: var(--weight-medium); white-space: nowrap; }
  .why-table__highlight { background: var(--color-accent-muted) !important; color: var(--color-text-primary) !important; }
  th.why-table__highlight { color: var(--color-accent) !important; }

  /* Personas */
  .why-personas { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--space-6); }
  .why-persona {
    padding: var(--space-6); background: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }
  .why-persona__role { font-size: var(--text-lg); font-weight: var(--weight-bold); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); color: var(--color-accent); }
  .why-persona__list { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-3); }
  .why-persona__list li {
    padding-left: var(--space-5); position: relative;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }
  .why-persona__list li::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.55em;
    width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* CTA */
  .why-cta { padding: var(--space-16) var(--space-6); text-align: center; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle); }
  .why-cta__inner { max-width: var(--content-width); margin: 0 auto; }
  .why-cta__title { font-size: var(--text-3xl); font-weight: var(--weight-bold); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .why-cta__desc { color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: var(--text-lg); margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
  .why-cta__desc code { color: var(--color-accent); background: var(--color-accent-muted); padding: 0.1em 0.4em; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); }
  .why-cta__buttons { display: flex; gap: var(--space-3); justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-6); font-size: var(--text-base); font-weight: var(--weight-medium); border-radius: var(--radius-md); text-decoration: none; transition: all var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out); }
  .btn--primary { background: var(--color-accent); color: #fff; }
  .btn--primary:hover { background: var(--color-accent-hover); color: #fff; }
  .btn--secondary { background: var(--color-surface-raised); color: var(--color-text-primary); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .btn--secondary:hover { background: var(--color-border); color: var(--color-text-primary); }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .why-personas { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .why-solution__item { flex-direction: column; }
  }
</style>
